// spec: RT-009, RT-010
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// RT-009 makes Val answer an Integer where the text has no point, so
// Val('42') is 42 and 'is Integer' is true.  RT-010 lets Max take any two
// numbers.  Together they make Max(Val(A), Val(B)) work.
//
// ⚠️ Individually each built-in is defensible; together they leave
// Max(Val(A), Val(B)) failing for EVERY input, which is why they are one
// defect and not two.

WriteLn (Val ('42'));
WriteLn (Val ('42') is Integer);
WriteLn (Val ('1.5'));

WriteLn (Max (Val ('3'), Val ('7')));
